{#- options: list of {value, label} with string values, and page: true on an option only the page offers, which the shell keeps when a pushed shared list lacks it; the one whose value is the string selected is chosen, none when it is null. Compared strictly, because a loose comparison would also choose "01" and "1.0" for "1", and a browser shows the last of several selected options. -#}
{%- for option in options %}
<option value="{{ option.value }}"{% if option.value is same as(selected) %} selected{% endif %}{% if option.page ?? false %} data-page-option{% endif %}>{{ option.label }}</option>
{%- endfor %}
